<title>FRANCE: Bertrand Faure '96 profits jump.</title>
<headline>Bertrand Faure '96 profits jump.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>  Net attributable			   303.2  vs	    92.3</p>
<p>  Net					    346.4  vs	   115.8</p>
<p>  Net attributable per share (francs)   17.7  vs	     5.6</p>
<p>  Operating				    726.2  vs	   481.7</p>
<p>  Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		 639.1  vs	   302.6</p>
<p>  Financial			    loss   87.1  vs    loss 179.1</p>
<p>  Cashflow				     926.4  vs	   659.3</p>
<p>  Net debt				     1,834  vs	   2,522</p>
<p>  Turnover				    13,871  vs	  12,532</p>
<p>  Net dividend (francs)			  4  vs	     NA</p>
<p>  Gross dividend (francs)			6	 up 14.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Automobile seat manufacturer Bernard Faure said in a statement that 1997 first-quarter turnover figures for automobile seats showed good progress over the comparable year earlier period and &quot;allow us to hope for a level of activity at least comparable to 1996 for the full year exercise.&quot; It said that Ratier-Figeac would see its turnover increase by a &quot;significant amount&quot; and luggage maker Delsey should &quot;reap the fruits of its industrial reorganisation and the launch of new products.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;All these factors, despite continued strong pressure on prices, should lead to another rise in profits for the group in 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>(( -- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ))</p>
